# Next.js 16 Architecture Rules — Aquarius DeFi Lab


## Core Principles
- Always use the App Router.
- Default to Server Components unless explicitly required otherwise.
- Prefer server-side data fetching and computation.
- Never use legacy Pages Router patterns.

## Data Fetching
- Use the `use cache` directive for all data-heavy fetches.
- Do not use manual revalidation unless explicitly required.
- Favor deterministic data flows over client-side fetching.

## React & Performance
- Assume React Compiler is enabled.
- Do NOT introduce useMemo or useCallback unless strictly necessary.
- Prefer simplicity and clarity over premature optimization.

## Forms & Mutations
- Use Server Actions for all mutations.
- Prefer `next/form` over custom form handlers.

## Routing & Rendering
- Enable Partial Prerendering (PPR) where applicable.
- Separate static shell from dynamic data regions.

## Code Quality
- Prefer explicitness over magic.
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions.
- Favor composability and long-term maintainability.

## Summary (Non-Negotiable)
- Always use the App Router (Next.js 16+).
- Default to Server Components unless explicitly told otherwise.
- Never add `use client` unless browser-only APIs are required.
- Use the React Compiler — do NOT add useMemo or useCallback.
- Use the `use cache` directive for all data-fetching utilities.
- Prefer Server Actions for mutations.
- Enable Partial Prerendering (PPR) where applicable.
- Never mix data-fetching logic inside UI components.
